--- log ---
2026-09-01T16:30Z claude created, child of 0550

2026-09-01T13:18Z MinhHaDuong note blocker 0552 closed — Blocked-by removed.

2026-09-01T18:22Z claude note BLOCKER #1 HAS A FIX WAITING, one level below where this ticket's round-2 review diagnosed it. Ticket 0567 (closed 2026-09-01, fork branch `t0567-ledger-ownership-guard` off `tranche-2-conductor-election`) gives `Ledger.markDone`/`markFailed` the compare-and-swap `claim()` always had: guarded on `claimed_by` AND `claimed_input`, returning whether the write applied. The clobber this ticket's review reproduced against `ExtractStage.putExtractState` is prevented in the shared primitive, so every stage gets it rather than each stage re-deriving it. WHAT THIS TICKET STILL OWES WHEN IT RESUMES: (a) adopt the new signatures — `markDone(wid, holder, claimedInput)` is now required, so `ExtractStage` will not compile until it passes its holder, deliberately; (b) decide what a rejected completion does at the stage level, since 0567 only reports it — the ledger returns false, and what the extract stage should do with a document it finished for a row it no longer owns is this ticket's call, not the primitive's; (c) `putExtractState` writes the extract-side row and is NOT covered by 0567 — it needs the same guard or must be folded into the guarded completion, whichever this ticket judges right; (d) blocker #2, the truncation sibling case (a stream cut after `content` closes but before the trailing page-count fields), is untouched by any of this and has no ticket of its own — it stays this ticket's.
--- body ---
## Context

Third tranche (tracker 0550): the first pipeline worker. Sequential
extract, run-to-drain, FIFO within class — no lanes, no bands yet. The
§5.2.3 class order (metadata > notes/annotations > body) is an ORDER BY
and arrives here for free.

## Relevant files

- SPEC.md §5.2.4 (shim split: bookkeeping conductor-side, the
  whole-document GET worker-side; back-off ratified 2026-09-01),
  §5.2.3 (classes, first-with-text), DECISIONS.md 2026-09-01 (back-off
  ruling).

## Actions

1. Extract worker: spawned on queue work, drains, exits; one document
   GET at a time, nice 19 + background I/O class where the platform
   exposes one (per the ruling's capability wording).
2. Class order in the dispatch query; first-with-text choice function
   with stored skip reasons.
3. Latency back-off: rising local-API latency median inserts a decaying
   delay between fetches; reported on the instrument panel. No Web-API
   fallback (ticket 0505 is separate).
4. Activity-file yield between documents.

## Test

- Red first: against the replay fixture with programmed latency ramp,
  the inter-fetch delay appears and decays; without the ramp, none.

## Verification

- [ ] Per item, nothing has body text extracted before its record
      bookkeeping exists (class order, per SPEC's per-item assertion)
- [ ] Worker exits on stdin EOF and on lease-holder mismatch

## Invariants

- Politeness constraints (web transport) untouched; upstream tests green.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Extract stage merged on a fork branch, back-off test green
